      "sector": "public_sector",
      "title": "CREDEBL: An Open-Source Digital Trust Infrastructure Enabling Trusted Digital Ecosystems",
      "summary": "CREDEBL is an open-source Digital Public Good contributed by AYANWORKS under LFDT.\n\nA. Bhutan NDI:\nBhutan NDI, led by Druk Holding & Investments Limited (DHI), enables citizens to receive, store & share digital credentials. Bhutan faced long travel distances, paper identity, manual verification & limited interoperability. Bhutan NDI adopted CREDEBL as its foundational layer for National Digital Identity Foundational Credentials & Verifiable Credentials. Citizens use digital wallets to share required information with consent, while service providers verify credentials. Built on W3C and OpenID4VC standards, CREDEBL enables interoperable, privacy-preserving trust. Bhutan NDI serves 525000+ users.\n\nB. Digi Yatra:\nDigi Yatra Foundation’s IATA Contactless Travel PoC with IndiGo, SITA & BLR Airport demonstrated International e-Passport Digital Travel Credentials on CREDEBL. Digi Yatra enables paperless airport travel using digital identity. CREDEBL provides the foundational layer for secure issuance, sharing & verification, ensuring privacy, cryptographic trust and global interoperability. The PoC aligned with IATA standards & produced the first International e-Passport credential holder.",
